{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1777130870,"nonce":"8K+2+c++h1fbzWD7NvrO3k8b+T0=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABAf_wXQ","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/86","origin":"github"},"title":"Test: independent per-thruster steer+throttle via two-joystick RC passthrough","message":"## Goal\n\nDrive BizzyBoat with two joysticks — one per thruster, each commanding both\nthrottle and steering angle of its thruster independently — to characterize\nwhat the boat can do (crab, pivot in place, asymmetric thrust) before\ndeciding what kind of mixing the autonomy stack should learn to do.\n\n## Background\n\nBizzyBoat physically has **two steerable thrusters** but the FCU is currently\nconfigured to treat them as **one virtual steerable thruster**. From\n`config/fcu/bizzyboat_fcu_baseline.param`:\n\n```\nFRAME_CLASS      2     # Boat\nFRAME_TYPE       0     # Undefined\nSERVO1_FUNCTION  70    # Throttle  (mirrored to both thruster ESCs)\nSERVO2_FUNCTION  70    # Throttle\nSERVO3_FUNCTION  26    # Steering  (mirrored to both steering servos)\nSERVO4_FUNCTION  26    # Steering\nMOT_VEC_ANGLEMAX 0     # Vectored thrust disabled\n```\n\nThe mirroring is intentional — both thrusters get the same throttle and the\nsame angle. Per ArduRover docs, there is no stock frame type for \"twin\nazimuth thrusters with independent per-thruster steering\" (Vectored Thrust\nin ArduRover means a single steering servo aiming both motors together;\nOmni frames are fixed-orientation throttle-only).\n\n## Approach: 4-param RC passthrough flip\n\nSmallest reversible change to the FCU config:\n\n```\nSERVO1_FUNCTION  1   # RCPassThru  (was 70)\nSERVO2_FUNCTION  1   # RCPassThru  (was 70)\nSERVO3_FUNCTION  1   # RCPassThru  (was 26)\nSERVO4_FUNCTION  1   # RCPassThru  (was 26)\n```\n\nThen RC inputs 1–4 pass straight through to SERVO outputs 1–4 with no\nmixer in between. From ROS, publish `mavros_msgs/OverrideRCIn` driven by a\nsmall dual-joystick node (left stick → port thruster throttle+angle;\nright stick → starboard thruster throttle+angle).\n\nArduPilot stays in MANUAL mode. Arming, RC failsafe, and the safety\nswitch all still work. Reverting is one parameter reload.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [ ] Save current params to a timestamped file before flipping\n- [ ] Bench test on jackstands: confirm each of the 4 channels moves\n      its expected actuator and only that one\n- [ ] Confirm `OverrideRCIn` release sentinel (PWM=0) hands control\n      back to the radio cleanly\n- [ ] Water test, low throttle limits, spotter, radio kill-switch ready\n- [ ] Try: parallel translation, pivot in place, asymmetric thrust\n      (one full forward, one full reverse), crab toward a target\n- [ ] Capture rosbag of `OverrideRCIn` + `mavros/rc/out` + IMU + GPS\n- [ ] Restore baseline params; verify boat returns to normal\n      single-virtual-thruster behavior\n\n## Known caveats\n\n- **Override timeout:** ArduPilot reverts to RC stick input if the\n  override stream stops. Publish at 10–50 Hz and use PWM=0 (release)\n  on shutdown.\n- **Arming gate still applies** — disarmed = trim outputs regardless\n  of what we publish.\n- **No mixer means no mixer-based failsafes.** Treat the test like a\n  manual radio test: spotter, kill-switch on the transmitter, conservative\n  throttle limits.\n- **Document the param save/restore cycle in the deployment log**\n  (`docs/bizzyboat_deployment_log.md`) — don't trust memory after a\n  long bench session.\n\n## Helm message redesign — explicitly out of scope here\n\nA two-joystick test is exploratory. For this issue, drive\n`OverrideRCIn` directly from a small joystick node, or use\n`std_msgs/Float32MultiArray` if an internal layer split is wanted.\nThe question of whether `marine_interfaces/msg/Helm` should be\nwidened to multiple channels (or replaced by a standard message\nlike `control_msgs/MultiDOFCommand`) is **tabled until the test\ntells us what mixing semantics the autonomy stack actually wants**.\nFiling a follow-up issue then will be cheaper than designing the\nmessage now.\n\n## Also out of scope\n\n- On-FCU Lua mixing (Script1..4 functions). This is the right path\n  if/when we want autonomy-driven per-thruster control with FCU\n  failsafes intact, but it's a much bigger change than what this\n  issue is for.\n- ros2_control modeling of the thrusters as joints.\n- ArduPilot frame-class changes.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null}]}